    78	
    79	| New | File |
    80	|-----|------|
    81	| `dao.stream.rpc.client` | `src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/client.cljc` |
    82	| `dao.stream.rpc.server` | `src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/server.cljc` |
    83	| `dao.stream.rpc.ws` | `src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc` |
    84	| `yin.repl.core` | `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc` |
    85	| `yin.repl.driver` | `src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc` |
    86	| `yin.repl` | `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` |
    87	| `yin.repl.runner` | `src/clj/yin/repl/runner.clj` |
    88	
    89	`dao.stream`, `dao.stream.ringbuffer` and `dao.stream.ws` are the
    90	sibling plan's deliverables. The cljd half of `dao.stream.ws` is this plan's,
    91	per *Prerequisites*.
    92	
    93	**Build configuration.** `deps.edn` gains `:clj-yin-repl`,
    94	`:cljs-yin-repl`, `:cljd-yin-repl` and `:cljd-yin-repl-build` beside
    95	the existing set. But `:cljs-yin-repl` is only
    96	`shadow.cljs.devtools.cli run yin.repl/-main`, which executes a Clojure function
    97	on the JVM; the Node REPL is the `:yin-repl` **`:node-script`** build in
    98	`shadow-cljs.edn`. So the cljs deliverable needs a `:yin-repl` build added
    99	there. **This is the one edit to an existing file this plan makes**: it is
   100	purely additive, touches no existing build, and there is no way to define a
   101	shadow build without it. `bin/` gains a v2 Dart entry importing
   102	`lib/cljd-out/yin/repl.dart`, since `runner.clj:13` runs
   103	`bin/yin_repl_main.dart` rather than the alias's `:output-dir`.
   104	
   105	**cljd file layout, decided now.** v1's precedent is a *shadow*
   106	`src/cljd/dao/stream/ws.cljd` hand-synced with the `.cljc`, because a single
   107	`.cljc` leaks `:clj` branches into cljd's host-eval pass. `#?(:clj …)` does not
   108	exclude code from the cljd build; `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)` with `:cljd` **first**
   109	is required, and `:cljd` in tail position silently fails. Every new `.cljc` file
   110	here is written that way from the start, and full cljd namespace compilation is
   111	a gate on each phase. The verbatim copy from `yin/repl.cljc` contains bare
   112	`#?(:clj …)` blocks (lines 63, 836 among others) that must be rewritten as they
   113	are copied; a shadow `.cljd` is the fallback if any file resists.
   114	
   115	**On duplication.** `yin.repl` cannot share code with `yin.repl`, because
   116	sharing would mean editing it, and the helpers are `defn-` so they cannot be
   117	reached anyway. Reviewers disagreed on the size — one counted ~350 of 1085 lines
   118	as verbatim-copyable, another 620–680 — and agreed on the shape: **the split is
   119	sync versus async, not stream versus non-stream.** Functions that straddle
   120	include `emit-output!` (113), `make-repl-primitives` (120), `make-vm` (160),
   121	`create-state` (175, inline `{:position 0}` cursors), `stream-status` and
   122	`repl-state` (213–299, uses `ds/closed?`), the `collect-*` and `finalize-eval`
   123	chain (381–451), `eval-datoms` (454), `handle-command` (552), and the whole
   124	`eval-input` chain (652–731).
   125	
   126	R2's first deliverable is therefore a **function-level inventory** of all 1085
   127	lines marked *copy verbatim*, *copy and adapt*, or *rewrite*. `yin.repl.core`
   128	holds the verbatim set; `yin.repl` holds the rest. Guessing the boundary is
   129	what produced the wrong estimate twice.
