     1	(ns yang.clojure
     2	  "Yang Clojure compiler - Compiles Clojure code into Yin VM Universal AST.
     3	
     4	  This is the Clojure-specific compiler in the Yang compiler collection.
     5	  It transforms Clojure s-expressions into the Universal AST format that
     6	  the Yin VM can execute. It handles:
     7	  - Literals (numbers, strings, booleans, nil, collections)
     8	  - Variables (symbols)
     9	  - Lambda expressions (fn)
    10	  - Function application (including stream operations via module system)
    11	  - Conditionals (if)
    12	  - Let bindings (let)
    13	  - Top-level definitions via explicit yin/def store effects
    14	  - Macro definitions (defmacro) and macro call sites (:yin/macro-expand)
    15	
    16	  Macro support:
    17	  - defmacro is a special form that lowers to (def name (lambda params body)) with
    18	    :yin/macro? true. It is NOT a regular application.
    19	  - compile-program threads a compile-time macro-env set. When (defmacro name ...)
    20	    is processed, name is added to the env for subsequent forms.
    21	  - Macro call sites emit {:type :yin/macro-expand :operator {:type :variable :name op} ...}
    22	    The yin.vm macro expander resolves the variable reference to the lambda EID.
    23	
    24	  Stream operations (stream/make, stream/put, stream/take, >!, <!) are compiled
    25	  as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.
    26	
    27	  The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js."
    28	  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile]))
    29	
    30	
