   477	## Boundary of this plan
   478	
   479	**Untouched** — no edits, no deletions, no deprecation markers: `dao.stream.cljc`
   480	and everything under `src/cljc/dao/stream/`; `yin/repl.cljc`,
   481	`src/clj/yin/repl/runner.clj`, `src/cljd/yin/repl/flutter.cljd`; their tests;
   482	the existing `deps.edn` aliases and `shadow-cljs.edn` builds. `dao.jing.remote`
   483	keeps working on v1 and gets its own plan; it is the harder migration, since its
   484	`call!` is synchronous-on-JVM and `jing/materialize!` and `jing/get` dispatch
   485	through it as ordinary value-returning calls.
   486	
   487	**Deliberately out of this slice:** remote telemetry over `ws://`, a second ws
   488	client that proves nothing `connect` does not; the `:semantic`, `:register` and
   489	`:stack` evaluators, which follow in the VM plan; chain-forwarding through a
   490	server's own remote (D4); the Flutter widget; `retry`, `dedup` and a v2 UDP
   491	transport; ws-level resumption; flow control; and authentication — `--host
   492	127.0.0.1` remains the only boundary, as in v1.
   493	
   494	## End condition
   495	
   496	Complete when, on each of clj, cljs (Node) and cljd, a v2 REPL server accepts a
   497	connection from a second process, evaluates forms sent to it, and survives a
   498	disconnect and reattach — with `yin.repl` requiring no v1 namespace, which
   499	running on `yin.vm` makes true rather than aspirational. R5's four facts plus
   500	the cross-host pair are the test.
   501	
   502	Coexistence is the expected end state. Both REPLs ship, both alias sets work,
   503	and `dao.stream.rpc.*` keeps serving `dao.jing.remote`. Deleting v1 is the
   504	stream plan's end condition, when its last consumer has migrated — of which this
   505	is the first.
