## Findings

1. **P1 | [yin.vm.implementation-plan.md:62](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.implementation-plan.md:62) | “Six v1 idioms” cover the port | Replace this with a full semantic-redesign inventory.**  
   The list misses dependencies on features that v2 explicitly removes:

   - `dao.runtime` uses waiter registration at [runtime.cljc:156](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:156) and [runtime.cljc:181](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:181), destructive `drain-one!` at [runtime.cljc:94](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:94), `closed?` at [runtime.cljc:115](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:115), and transport-produced `:woke` entries at [runtime.cljc:97](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:97), [runtime.cljc:125](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:125), and [runtime.cljc:219](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:219).
   - `engine` repeats the same assumptions: fabricated cursor internals at [engine.cljc:168](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:168) and [engine.cljc:191](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:191), waiters at [engine.cljc:442](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:442), destructive take at [engine.cljc:208](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:208), and close wakeups at [engine.cljc:230](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:230).
   - The contract explicitly has no waiter extension, destructive read, or `closed?`: [dao.stream.md:184](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:184), [dao.stream.md:501](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:501), [dao.stream.md:575](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:575).

   `dao.runtime` is therefore not a leaf whose “single reference” merely moves, contrary to [the plan:138](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.implementation-plan.md:138). Specify a polling wait-set, store opaque cursors rather than positions, remove all wake metadata, make close observation arise from subsequent operations, and either remove `:stream/take` from v2 or define it above DaoStream as an explicit interpreter with its own cursor.

2. **P1 | [yin.vm.implementation-plan.md:33](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.implementation-plan.md:33) | The ten namespaces plus `yin.module` are the complete closure and “nothing dangles” | Add `dao.stream.ringbuffer` as a direct dependency and correct the creation call.**  
